(a) Equal access  
All individuals shall have the right to fully and equally access goods, services, facilities, benefits, and accommodations at any public establishment as defined herein, without discrimination or segregation based on race, color, religion, or national origin.  

(b) Places of public accommodation affecting interstate commerce or supported by State action  
The following types of businesses that serve the public are considered places of public accommodation within the meaning of this subchapter if their operations impact interstate commerce, or if discriminatory practices by them are supported by actions of the State:  

(1) Any hotel, motel, or other lodging establishment that provides temporary accommodations to guests, excluding those with no more than five rental rooms which are actually lived in by the owner;  

